{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/755328-when-is-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-set","id":755328,"title":"When is Werewolf 20th Anniversary Edition Set?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-04T17:41:06-08:00","id":755328,"title":"When is Werewolf 20th Anniversary Edition Set?","content":"I had a long involvement with the Classic World of Darkness and was...emotional...about the way that the line came to an end. Some friends sent me looking at Onyx Path recently, saying that I'd like what I see. My biggest question is when things are taking place in the books. Is this all pre-Apocalypse/Gehenna? Or post?<br /> Thanks so much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9106-jimflory","name":"jimflory","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T17:44:32-08:00","id":755364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jimflory</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/755328-when-is-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-set#post755328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a long involvement with the Classic World of Darkness and was...emotional...about the way that the line came to an end. Some friends sent me looking at Onyx Path recently, saying that I'd like what I see. My biggest question is when things are taking place in the books. Is this all pre-Apocalypse/Gehenna? Or post?<br /> Thanks so much!</div> </div> </div> </div>Pre-Apocalypse, and also whenever you want it to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T22:32:09-08:00","id":755847,"title":"","content":"The 20th edition books, in general, are meant to be sort of omnibus editions, covering everything from 1e through Revised in terms of setting and plot. As such there's kind of time agnostic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T00:06:34-08:00","id":755942,"title":"","content":"Also, they seem to be saying the Apocalypse is coming, but it doesn't seem as inevitable and urgent as it was towards the end of the line. There is even a new line in the prophecy of Phoenix. One about Hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T00:12:11-08:00","id":755947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/755328-when-is-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-set?p=755942#post755942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, they seem to be saying the Apocalypse is coming, but it doesn't seem as inevitable and urgent as it was towards the end of the line. There is even a new line in the prophecy of Phoenix. One about Hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>That hope is actually half-life 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T02:26:23-08:00","id":756057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/755328-when-is-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-set?p=755947#post755947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That hope is actually half-life 3</div> </div> </div> </div>You unbeliever! When Half Life 3 is out, you will see... you will all seeeeeeeee...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T11:12:23-08:00","id":756952,"title":"","content":"It's strange, these nostalgia editions seem to cater to that 90s Gothic Punk atmosphere and the setting should feel and mostly behave like that; but with a touch of anachronism in that things like smartphones or the economical crisis are shown in art and mentioned in setting description (in the introductory comic some Pentex grunt sends a pic of a magical glyph with a phone)<br /> Ultimately as already told they are set whenever you want them to be, but I think the default assumption is 2010+<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T13:09:48-08:00","id":757154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vidyaraja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/755328-when-is-werewolf-20th-anniversary-edition-set?p=756952#post756952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's strange, these nostalgia editions seem to cater to that 90s Gothic Punk atmosphere and the setting should feel and mostly behave like that; but with a touch of anachronism in that things like smartphones or the economical crisis are shown in art and mentioned in setting description (in the introductory comic some Pentex grunt sends a pic of a magical glyph with a phone)<br /> Ultimately as already told they are set whenever you want them to be, but I think the default assumption is 2010+</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree on the tone. Werewolf is distinctly in its revised tone which has a lot more cultural research and reasoning about logical consequences of things like how the Garou work. It's very early 2000's in its tone and very different from the Gothic Punk roots of the old WoD. Heck, I'd say that 2nd edition had already moved away from Gothic, and Revised dropped a lot of the puerile cheap enviromentalism for better thought out context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8760,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","user":"Cogliostro","date":". 11-05-2015, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T10:59:27-08:00","id":761607,"title":"","content":"W20 is set in the modern day, but the metaplot has been 'rolled back' to mid-2nd edition or so. The Seventh Generation are still around (though they have updated for the times), the Stargazers are still with the Garou Nation, the resistance against Black Tooth is still taking shape, and Albrecht has yet to claim the Silver Crown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T02:14:58-08:00","id":762115,"title":"","content":"Actually the Black Tooth thing is open ended. The Changing Breeds present it as either a done deal or something that's being done right now. In general the whole thing has a very toolboxy approach to what's going on plot wise. And I couldn't be happier <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T12:25:25-08:00","id":768008,"title":"","content":"Thanks folks!<br /> Follow-up question; is the 20th edition suitable for running/playing in a Dark Ages or Wild West Werewolf game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9106-jimflory","name":"jimflory","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T13:09:50-08:00","id":768048,"title":"","content":"There's no real information in the main W20 book for doing so; but it doesn't take much. W20 already has a Wild West Expansion, and if you have any of the old Wild West Werewolf books, the vast majority of the fluff still applies. If you have either of the DA Werewolf books, it wouldn't be hard to fill in the blanks as it were (Revised would be easier).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}